# Pit Trap sacrifices itself for two mana and destroys a nonflying attacker despite a regeneration shield; a flier is illegal (CR 701.8, 701.19).
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Pit Trap
Island x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Drudge Skeletons
Ornithopter
Memnite
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pit Trap.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Drudge Skeletons.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Attackers]
Bot2.Attack(Drudge Skeletons > Bot1; Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Pit Trap.Activate(Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Pit Trap.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Battlefield.Pit Trap.Activate(Drudge Skeletons)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Choose(Tap Pit Trap)
? Bot1.Graveyard.Pit Trap.Colors =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Drudge Skeletons.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
